<article class="env-definition" id="02MR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02MR">Definition <span data-tag="02MR">12.10.5</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$, $\mathcal{B}$ be abelian categories. Let $F : \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{B}$ be an exact functor. Then the full subcategory of objects $C$ of $\mathcal{A}$ such that $F(C) = 0$ is called the <em>kernel of the functor $F$</em>, and is sometimes denoted $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(F)$. </p>
</article>